Hi Dan,

Thanks! So to clarify (before I read it J), you simultaneously had GVS going on in BOTH detection and occupancy parts of the model?

My structure now is to do MODEL selection, that is I use a categorical distribution to choose a row of a binary matrix, i.e., a binary vector that specifies the model which allows a straightforward prior for the MODELS.

So Im wondering if I do them separately, using two model matrices (one for p one for psi) or one big one where the categorical variable selects a [psi+p] model.

C

