Yep, I had a dynamic, multi-state occupancy model with covariates on 2 state processes and the detection process.  So the GVS was working simultaneously, or jointly, on both parts of the model.

My impression of the model selection approach you describe is that the sampler can get stuck and not jump between models as much as you would desire.  I don't have experience with it though.  I do know that BUGS/JAGS can be somewhat unfriendly to certain applications of categorical distributions, especially in terms of speed.

