I have done something similar to what Daniel describes with indicator variables. In my case, I also did a simultaneous variable selection for both components of the model. With a bit of manipulation of the posterior results of the MCMC, I have got model rankings based on the posterior model probabilities.

I also do variable selection routinely, although I have to admit that it can be very slow in JAGS if the model structure is complicated. For example, today I ran a complex model with three levels for 500 data points and six continuous covariates, and it took 8 hours in my laptop (3 chains, 4000,000 iterations). It was not an occupancy model, though.

Cheers

Pablo

