Terriffic. Thanks everyone.
Back to joint GVS it is.

By the way, the reason I liked the product space approach is that for a model set with a handful of covariates , including interactions, specification of a uniform prior on the model set is straightforward and makes sense. For GVS I suppose I need to rescale the priors to accommodate the fact that fixed effect need to be included when interaction terms are present.

Thanks all

Chris

